Feature: Keycloak Realm Setup Readiness
  As an operator starting the app, the checks target, the local stack, or a deploy
  I want the realm setup to wait for Keycloak's admin login to be ready
  So that start-up no longer stops on a Keycloak that reports itself healthy before its admin login is usable

  Background:
    Given the realm setup performs an admin login and a first admin call against the Keycloak admin endpoint

  # Why: "the first admin login in the realm setup ... gets 503 Service Unavailable ... Make the realm setup wait for Keycloak to be ready: retry the admin login and the first admin call only on 503"
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The readiness wait covers only the admin login and the first admin call; subsequent realm-configuration calls do not need their own readiness wait
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] The retry uses a back-off interval and growth policy within the 2-minute budget
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Realm setup succeeds after Keycloak answers 503 a few times before it is ready
    Given a local Keycloak that answers the first few admin login attempts with 503 Service Unavailable and then serves successfully
    When the realm setup runs the admin login and the first admin call
    Then the realm setup completes with a successful exit status
    And the realm is reported as configured
    And the realm setup reports that more than one login attempt was made

  # Why: "the first admin login in the realm setup ... or a refused connection, and the whole start-up stops"
  @key-example
  Scenario: Realm setup succeeds after a refused connection before Keycloak is ready
    Given a local Keycloak that refuses the first few admin login connections and then serves successfully
    When the realm setup runs the admin login and the first admin call
    Then the realm setup completes with a successful exit status
    And the realm is reported as configured
    And the realm setup reports that more than one login attempt was made

